        "@id": "urn:lost-library:object%3Ampo-1385"
      },
      "status": "unresolved",
      "basis": "researcher_interpretation",
      "polarity": "positive",
      "attributedTo": {
        "@id": "urn:lost-library:agent%3Aproject-ai"
      },
      "details": "{\"id\": \"claim:pair-98a6b3277c205d6a8aa7\", \"subject\": \"object:finn-iv173\", \"predicate\": \"same_codex\", \"object\": \"object:mpo-1385\", \"basis\": \"researcher_interpretation\", \"status\": \"unresolved\", \"source_stance\": \"suggested\", \"polarity\": \"positive\", \"attributed_to\": \"agent:project-ai\", \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-02\", \"source_statement_date\": null, \"scope\": \"book relationship\", \"provenance\": [{\"source\": \"source:36fb90793e201dc844e5\", \"locator\": \"H04\"}], \"supports\": [], \"challenges\": [], \"support_notes\": [\"The Finnish leaf contains a readable Te Deum passage in a large one-column music layout.\", \"E27 verifies that BOMPAC-9531 contains F.m.IV.173, Ant 242/Fr 29666 and Hy 49/Fr 25592. The official IV.173 record explicitly identifies Ant 242/Fr 29666 as same codex.\", \"Selected D initials in IV.173 and Fr 1385 show red stems and pale fields; the IV.173 D has visible red interior marks. The Fr 1385 photograph is too small for a reliable comparison of fine detail or exact mark count.\"], \"challenge_notes\": [\"Te Deum is widespread. Fr1385 has other liturgical material; contents neither prove nor disprove same codex.\", \"BOMPAC places Fr 1385 with IV.157 in unit 912, separate from IV.173 in unit 9531; this is a published reconstruction distinction, not proof against a shared production group or hand.\", \"The official Fragmenta catalogue describes IV.156 and IV.157 as stylistically similar but does not say they are the same codex; Codex 1505 is listed as a suggestion, while other links receive explicit same-codex labels.\", \"The literature-backed Fr 8201/8304 different-book pair also has D initials combining red stems and pale fields with ornamental marks. This counterexample means these broad features cannot establish one book. It does not prove that the IV.173/Fr 1385 pair are different books.\", \"Fr 1385 and Fr 20274 are assigned to the published IV.157/Ant 99 reconstruction. The two retained Fr 20274 views do not supply a comparably decorated D for this test; this is not a claim about the complete manuscript. Fr 29666, the stated IV.173 same-book comparator, has no local image.\", \"Unblinded, post-exposure, selected examples; unmatched exact chant roles and image quality; no population prevalence, discriminating accuracy or hand identification estimated.\"], \"source_locator\": null, \"contextual_evidence\": [\"evidence:O-mpo-1385\", \"evidence:O-finn-iv173-1-10\", \"evidence:V-1385-clipped-mark\"], \"lead_id\": \"pair-98a6b3277c205d6a8aa7\"}"
    },
