      "details": "{\"id\": \"claim:pair-0e5884ee8e7775c2a4ef\", \"subject\": \"object:mpo-10349\", \"predicate\": \"suggested_association\", \"object\": \"object:mpo-25592\", \"basis\": \"computational_suggestion\", \"status\": \"unresolved\", \"source_stance\": \"suggested\", \"polarity\": \"positive\", \"attributed_to\": \"agent:matcher\", \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-02\", \"source_statement_date\": null, \"scope\": \"book relationship\", \"provenance\": [{\"source\": \"source:340f945088b424d674d1\", \"locator\": \"pair-0e5884ee8e7775c2a4ef\"}], \"supports\": [], \"challenges\": [], \"support_notes\": [\"Saved compatibility ranking only; no new direct pair-level source interpretation was performed by this triage.\", \"Two narrow fields, with notated office material, prose rubrics and an All-Saints Jesu-salvator/redemptis-ope hymn candidate. / Notated hymn openings followed by continuous stanzas; A-patre-unigenitus cue and a Jesu-redemptor/verbum-patris candidate distinct from the selected10349 hymn.\"], \"challenge_notes\": [\"Shared style, liturgy, inherited metadata and capture appearance remain explanations; differing catalogue assignments are not automatic negatives.\", \"The published data assigns the objects to different reconstruction units; this is contextual counterevidence, not automatic proof of different books.\", \"Different sections, copying changes and composite volumes remain alternatives. Equal column counts or standard liturgical text are compatibility only. Incomplete photo/text coverage is not evidence of absence.\", \"The selected openings and continuations provisionally fit different known hymn texts rather than a diagnostic same-hymn variant. The first begins salvator/redemptis-ope, whereas the second has redemptor/verbum-patris context and the Tu-fabricator cue. This probable work mismatch defeats the proposed local textual correspondence; it does not exclude different sections in one historical volume.\"], \"source_locator\": null, \"contextual_evidence\": [], \"lead_id\": \"pair-0e5884ee8e7775c2a4ef\"}"
