      "details": "{\"id\": \"claim:pair-d3edceeb5829ddeac135\", \"subject\": \"object:mpo-10349\", \"predicate\": \"suggested_association\", \"object\": \"object:mpo-2862\", \"basis\": \"computational_suggestion\", \"status\": \"unresolved\", \"source_stance\": \"suggested\", \"polarity\": \"positive\", \"attributed_to\": \"agent:matcher\", \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-02\", \"source_statement_date\": null, \"scope\": \"book relationship\", \"provenance\": [{\"source\": \"source:340f945088b424d674d1\", \"locator\": \"pair-d3edceeb5829ddeac135\"}], \"supports\": [], \"challenges\": [], \"support_notes\": [\"Saved compatibility ranking only; no new direct pair-level source interpretation was performed by this triage.\"], \"challenge_notes\": [\"Shared style, liturgy, inherited metadata and capture appearance remain explanations; differing catalogue assignments are not automatic negatives.\", \"The published data assigns the objects to different reconstruction units; this is contextual counterevidence, not automatic proof of different books.\", \"The available10349 views show two narrow writing fields;2862 shows one broad music/text field, with rules crossing its reuse crease. The2863/2864 retained controls also have the broad design. This locally supports a layout distinction rather than explaining it solely by a reuse fold. The visible two-narrow-field versus one-broad-field designs support a local layout distinction and challenge an unchanged uniform copying layout. Exact original leaf/fold mapping and complete field-width calibration remain qualified. Composite volumes, mixed sections or copying changes can still explain one historical volume; same-codex identity remains unresolved.\"], \"source_locator\": null, \"contextual_evidence\": [], \"lead_id\": \"pair-d3edceeb5829ddeac135\"}"
