      "details": "{\"id\": \"claim:pair-d964f842625525837cb2\", \"subject\": \"object:mpo-10370\", \"predicate\": \"suggested_association\", \"object\": \"object:mpo-20274\", \"basis\": \"computational_suggestion\", \"status\": \"unresolved\", \"source_stance\": \"suggested\", \"polarity\": \"positive\", \"attributed_to\": \"agent:matcher\", \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-02\", \"source_statement_date\": null, \"scope\": \"book relationship\", \"provenance\": [{\"source\": \"source:340f945088b424d674d1\", \"locator\": \"pair-d964f842625525837cb2\"}], \"supports\": [], \"challenges\": [], \"support_notes\": [\"Saved compatibility ranking only; no new direct pair-level source interpretation was performed by this triage.\", \"All six retained target photographs and two selected8994 mark controls were inspected.10370's already recorded ij/II and k-like marks are visible again.20274 has a red upper-margin glyph whose reading/function remain uncertain, and a later pencil identifier corresponding to its catalogue reference. No secure comparable original address was recovered across this pair.\"], \"challenge_notes\": [\"Shared style, liturgy, inherited metadata and capture appearance remain explanations; differing catalogue assignments are not automatic negatives.\", \"The published data assigns the objects to different reconstruction units; this is contextual counterevidence, not automatic proof of different books.\", \"The available images do not establish a shared original folio/quire address or a conflicting address. Similar red ink, punctuation and k-like shape within the wider group are compatible with several books using a shared convention. An unread sign, different addresses and later identifiers cannot decide same-codex identity. The historical relationship stays unresolved.\"], \"source_locator\": null, \"contextual_evidence\": [], \"lead_id\": \"pair-d964f842625525837cb2\"}"
