      "details": "{\"id\": \"claim:pair-00f7a4ed7b39e57ed29e\", \"subject\": \"object:mpo-8072\", \"predicate\": \"suggested_association\", \"object\": \"object:mpo-8073\", \"basis\": \"computational_suggestion\", \"status\": \"unresolved\", \"source_stance\": \"suggested\", \"polarity\": \"positive\", \"attributed_to\": \"agent:matcher\", \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-02\", \"source_statement_date\": null, \"scope\": \"book relationship\", \"provenance\": [{\"source\": \"source:340f945088b424d674d1\", \"locator\": \"pair-00f7a4ed7b39e57ed29e\"}], \"supports\": [], \"challenges\": [], \"support_notes\": [\"Saved compatibility ranking only; no new direct pair-level source interpretation was performed by this triage.\", \"Invitatory Regem virginum cue and two Veni sponsa occurrences with short in-eternum versus longer pro-cuius-amore continuations. / Explicit Super magnificat antiphona rubric and blocks of continuous verse-like text alongside notated passages.\", \"Fr 8073 capture 3 has a Magnificat antiphon rubric and provisionally reads Felix terra pariens ... fons divinitatis ... reos a peccatis solvens duc ad patriam summae claritatis, matching the text indexed as Cantus 201813. The reading is reference-assisted and provisional.\", \"Fr 8073 capture 4 provisionally reads Annam filiam Abrahe que fulsit ex Aaron stirpe, identifying the second stanza of De stella sol oriturus, already catalogued as AH 52 no.104.\", \"The bottom text of capture 2 provisionally ends Ex hac car-; the top text of capture 3 begins nis planta surgit virgo sancta. The combined phrase fits the same stanza of Lucis huius festa. These are images attributed by the existing manifest to the same catalogue object.\", \"Capture 1 provisionally contains Funde vinum desolatis, the Liberalis liberali verse and an Ut de cue. Capture 2 appears to begin with Gloria patri and another Ut de cue before Lucis huius festa. Their arrangement is compatible with successive parts of a responsory, not proven photo overlap.\"], \"challenge_notes\": [\"Shared style, liturgy, inherited metadata and capture appearance remain explanations; differing catalogue assignments are not automatic negatives.\", \"BOMPAC-4861 includes the published8201/8304 different-book control. The unit cannot serve as independent same-codex ground truth for its other member pairs.\", \"The known8201/8304 different-book pair also shares the observed general ruling/layout; this feature cannot establish the candidate identity. The selected surviving contexts do not establish a complete corresponding diagnostic passage. Different feasts/genres and shared generic cues do not exclude one book. This is not an exhaustive chant census or a claim of no possible correspondence.\", \"AH 52 no.104's OCR base text gives quae ex Aaron stirpe fulsit; Piwoński 1985 p.305 prints quae fulsit ex Aaron stirpe, agreeing with the provisional local reading. The two edited texts and Swedish photograph have not been independently checked against their underlying original witnesses.\", \"Source readings are unblinded, reference-exposed and not independently reviewed. Source capture 1 lacks native resolution. We did not establish the medieval side sequence, inspect an external medieval exemplar, locate the printed baseline images, or identify the specific exemplar behind Piwoński's edited line. Prior notice of the antiphon in Fr 8073 remains unverified.\", \"AH 52 no.101 and a Cantus indexed Zutphen 6 f.246r inventory list the same six stanza openings in this order; Kelemen's published Tolnai breviary transcription presents a different order. These do not establish book identity or independent confirmation of the Swedish reading.\", \"Text selection and reading were reference-exposed and unreviewed. The catalogue claims one leaf, but the actual original side or quire mapping, photographic folding and composite/duplicate possibilities have not been independently resolved. The 1909 edition supplies prior art; no source-exemplar image was inspected.\", \"Cantus Index identifies Funde vinum 600932 and its Liberalis verse 600932a; a search-indexed Spis antiphonal inventory lists the responsory, verse and a Gloria verse in order. The inventory's special doxology is not attributed to Fr 8073. AH 5 no.34 also prints responsory and verse together.\", \"Reference-exposed AI reading; capture 1 is an 800-pixel thumbnail and the folds hide text. Two Ut de cues occur in different visible contexts, so they cannot safely be treated as common ink. Repeated text, intervening material, side and fold alternatives are unresolved.\", \"Schnabel's published Lübeck Ms. theol. lat. 2° 48a description lists AH 5 no.34 second nocturn responsory 3 with verse and Gloria, then Lucis huius festa AH 52 no.101, followed by Felix terra. AH 5 identifies the referenced responsory and verse as Funde vinum and Liberalis liberali. This is a separate surviving book.\", \"The described sequence is a concrete different-book control against a unique-book inference from the proposed Swedish sequence. The catalogue alone does not establish exact adjacency, complete text, identical melodies, transmission or a relationship between the books.\", \"Lübeck catalogue description read as a full search-indexed result; direct catalogue open and its facsimile resolver returned cache misses. No original Lübeck manuscript image or printed edition page image was inspected. Source descriptions and AH work identifiers are attributed, not direct independent readings of the Swedish fragment.\"], \"source_locator\": null, \"contextual_evidence\": [], \"lead_id\": \"pair-00f7a4ed7b39e57ed29e\"}"
    },
