-4-native.jpg\", \"selector\": {\"type\": \"FragmentSelector\", \"conformsTo\": \"http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/\", \"value\": \"xywh=350,1550,530,155\"}}, \"fragment_id\": \"mpo-9620\", \"source_url\": \"https://lbiiif.riksarkivet.se/arkis!R1009620_00004/full/max/0/default.jpg\", \"sha256\": \"053e4da7c3dd9c3cb29a867804bfc8f8f854b085b45960937944bb6744a606b3\", \"image_dimensions\": [949, 1718], \"rights_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/\", \"literal_candidate\": \"dixit uere locus iste sa[...]\", \"normalized_candidate\": null, \"observer\": \"Codex AI exploratory manual source reading; not independent or blind\", \"independent_confirmation\": false, \"interpretation_limits\": [\"No full corresponding work ID, local service position, complete melody or absolute pitch.\", \"No exact rhythmic values, chromatic inflections or audio realization.\", \"Ordinary ornament, differing verse/work context, section alternatives, multiple hands and composite books remain possible.\", \"No new matching score, threshold, performance metric, independent confirmation or novelty clearance.\"], \"note_position_record\": \"research/continuation_46/readings.v2.json\"}, \"independent_confirmation\": false}, {\"id\": \"evidence:I49-8304-rubric\", \"type\": \"EvidenceRegion\", \"basis\": \"project_observation\", \"attributed_to\": \"agent:project-ai\", \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-02\", \"annotation_id\": \"I49-8304-rubric\", \"image\": \"image:data/images/mpo-8304-capture-4.jpg\", \"target\": {\"source\": \"data/images/mpo-8304-capture-4.jpg\", \"selector\": {\"type\": \"FragmentSelector\", \"conformsTo\": \"http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/\", \"value\": \"xywh=330,270,260,125\"}}, \"sha256\": \"819f3dd18443e352d4162249aae929ff4b34fcc6cc1913e79dff267d11550529\", \"observation\": \"An actual Catherine/service heading precedes the opening chant. This supports the8304 side of the published office-opening premise; it supplies no second local opening on8201. Reference-exposed reading; saint and feriales are visible; bracketed abbreviation expansions remain editorial.\", \"literal_candidate\": \"De s[an]c[t]a kathe / rina sup[er] ps / feriales\", \"normalized_candidate\": \"De sancta Katherina super psalmos feriales\", \"source_url\": \"https://lbiiif.riksarkivet.se/v3/arkis!R1008304_00004/full/1000,/0/default.jpg\", \"import_date\": \"2026-11-02\", \"original_annotation\": {\"id\": \"I49-8304-rubric\", \"type\": \"Annotation\", \"motivation\": \"describing\", \"body\": {\"type\": \"TextualBody\", \"value\": \"An actual Catherine/service heading precedes the opening chant. This supports the8304 side of the published office-opening premise; it supplies no second local opening on8201. Reference-exposed reading; saint and feriales are visible; bracketed abbreviation expansions remain editorial.\", \"language\": \"en\"}, \"target\": {\"source\": \"data/images/mpo-8304-capture-4.jpg\", \"selector\": {\"type\": \"FragmentSelector\", \"conformsTo\": \"http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/\", \"value\": \"xywh=330,270,260,125\"}}, \"fragment_id\": \"mpo-8304\", \"source_url\": \"https://lbiiif.riksarkivet.se/v3/arkis!R1008304_00004/full/1000,/0/default.jpg\", \"sha256\": \"819f3dd18443e352d4162249aae929ff4b34fcc6cc1913e79dff267d11550529\", \"image_dimensions\": [1000, 697], \"rights_url\": \"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/\", \"literal_candidate\": \"De s[an]c[t]a kathe / rina sup[er] ps / feriales\", \"normalized_candidate\": \"De sancta Katherina super psalmos feriales\", \"observer\": \"Codex AI-assisted source recheck; reference exposed, no independent expert endorsement\", \"independent_confirmation\": false, \"interpretation_limits\": [\"All eight retained photographs were inspected, but they are multiple views of two fragments, not eight leaves or independent witnesses.\", \"No original-object review, complete diplomatic/chant transcription, full medieval-side map, repeated-office/composite adjudication, new exclusion or novelty clearance.\", \"The local visibility limit is not a refutation of the published rejection or evidence that a second beginning does not exist on the missing20106 source.\"]}, \"independent_confirmation\": false}, {\"id\": \"evidence:I49-8304-opening\", \"type\": \"EvidenceRegion\", \"basis\": \"project_observation\", \"attributed_to\": \"agent:project-ai\", \"recorded_at\": \"2026-11-02\", \"annotation_id\": \"I49-8304-opening\", \"image\": \"image:data/images/mpo-8304-capture-4.jpg\", \"target\": {\"source\": \"data/images/mpo-8304-capture-4.jpg\", \"selector\": {\"type\": \"FragmentSelector\", \"conformsTo\": \"http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/\", \"value\": \"xywh=205,310,660,155\"}}, \"sha256\": \"819f3dd18443e352d4162249aae929ff4b34fcc6cc1913e79dff267d11550529\", \"observation\": \"E69 supersedes E49 sollempnitas with provisional sollempni[a?]; consult I69-8304-opening-corrected. The large blue I starts the surviving Catherine opening text. The rubric and this incipit are one local context, not independent witnesses. Reference-exposed candidate transcription; spelling normalization is editorial and no exact external chant ID is assigned.\", \"literal_candidate\": \"Inclita sancte uirginis / katherine sollempni[a?] [...] (E69 re-reading)\", \"normalized_candidate\": \"Inclita sanctae virginis Katherinae sollemnia [...] (provisional E69 re-reading)\", \"source_url\": \"https://lbiiif.riksarkivet.se/v3/arkis!R1008304_00004/full/1000,/0/default.jpg\", \"import_date\": \"2026-11-02\", \"original_annotation\": {\"id\": \"I49-8304-opening\", \"type\": \"Annotation\", \"motivation\": \"describing\", \"body\": {\"type\": \"TextualBody\", \"value\": \"The large blue I starts the surviving Catherine opening text. The rubric and this incipit are one local context, not independent witnesses. Reference-exposed candidate transcription; spelling normalization is editorial and no exact external chant ID is assigned.\", \"language\": \"en\"}, \"target\": {\"source\"